						<div style="width:100%;">
							<p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 48pt; COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">Amyana Angeluv<?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /><o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <h1 style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt" align="center"><font face="Magik" color="#d3d3d3">Queen of Moonlite Redemption</font></h1> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 18pt; COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">&nbsp;<img src="/pics/1602/hierarchy/Amyana3.JPG" /></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><font color="#d3d3d3"></font><span style="FONT-SIZE: 18pt; COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"></p><font color="#d3d3d3"> <hr id="null" /> </font></span> <p><font color="#d3d3d3"></font></p><span style="FONT-SIZE: 18pt; COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"> <h1 style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">Amyana Angeluv<o:p></o:p></font></span></h1> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">An Interview by Vivicia<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">I am Vivicia, daughter of Guard Lucas and Issynal Angeluv, sister to Amyana Angeluv, and reporter for the Felwithe Times.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Upon learning of my background, my supervisors at the paper immediately wanted an interview with my sister.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Although not among the most powerful guild leaders, there are few that have not heard of her in some respect or another.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>My sister was always somewhat of a mystery to me, her ideas and thoughts were so expansive and seemingly impossible that, were it not for her enthusiam and determined nature, one would of thought her whimsical.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Due to her determined nature, I truly believe she could accomplish almost anything she set her mind to, although as her younger sister, it is possible that I am somewhat biased.<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">My mother and father had Amyana about five years before they had me.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I have few memories of my father, as he disappeared when I was about three years old.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>He left his post shortly after Amyana was born, but he couldn’t stay still for long.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Mother says that he had a mid-life crisis and was always chasing after one adventure or another.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>When he left for the last one I can’t help but to wonder if he knew, as he kissed the three of us goodbye, that he would not return.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I doubt he did, as these things are rarely foreseeable.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>We got postcards from him every week for the first couple months, but the postcards stopped.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>At home, my mother did her best, selling goods in her store.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Money was tight, and I imagine it was very hard on mother, taking care of the two of us, and worrying about the fate of her husband.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Shortly after reaching adolesence, Amyana left home.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>It wasn’t long at all before she started sending money home to us.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>This is were my story gets somewhat fuzzy, as I don’t know at all what she did once she left home.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Therefore, I chose to begin my interview with her starting on the day she left home.<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">I was pacing around the kitchen, waiting for her to come.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>She was running late, but I understood she was busy, and honestly I was grateful that she would take the time to allow me this interview.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>She visited us fairly often, but she was rarely able to stay long.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Someone would always need her for something somewhere.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>She came bursting through the door, with her red hair flying around her face, precisely fifteen minutes late.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I hugged her tightly, noticing a pain in her eyes I had not seen before.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>After a warm welcome, we sat down at the table and I clicked the small voice recorder on.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>She leaned back in her chair, crossed her legs and lazily brushed strand of the red locks from her face.<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">I cleared my throat, (I spoke to her in elven, but I’ll attempt to translate here) “Upon leaving home at the young age of sixteen, where did you go?”<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">She smiled, “To the Faydark of course”<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I laughed, the only way to leave Felwithe is through the Faydark!<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">I grinned at her, “Oh, you are a silly elf, where did you go after you left the Faydark?”<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">For a few minutes, she thought about the question, as if she was trying to remember exactly where she went.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Finally, she replied. “Well, I was wondering the Faydark, killing every random monster I happened across.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I was hoping to loot their corpses and aquire a small amount of platinum to send home.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>It was tedious, and I could barely come up with enough plantinum to eat, let alone send any home.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>One day, during a horrible rainstorm, I was hiding underneath the shelter provided by Kelethin above the Faydark, when I saw a figure walking toward me.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>It was hard to see through the rain at first, only allowing me to deciepher the siloutte of a man.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>As he came closer, he reached out his hand to me, and smiled, ‘My dear, you shall catch your death of cold here, you’re practically nude and dripping from head to toe.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Come, we will find you some warm food, and perhaps some better armor for your slender limbs.’<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I blushed profously, as indeed I was almost nude.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>My clothing had been almost ripped to shreds by a Basilik hatchling the prior evening.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>In the morning, the elven man finally identified himself as Terren Starwatcher.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I had heard talk of him before, he was a kind man, and a well respected Cleric.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I think it was this day I chose to become a Cleric.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Terren told me of the Sylvan Initiate Armor, and how to create some.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I rushed out immediately and started gathering the required materials.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I had a hard time finding some of the pieces…”<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">Her voice trailed off for a moment, then she leaned forward.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>In her eyes, I saw something that I still can not describe.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>She smiled, “It was dark, and I was running through the forest looking for a Giant Sylvan Bat.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I needed a fur from one for the final piece of the armor.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I was having such a wretched time finding one, I was getting really frustrated.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Suddenly, I looked up and saw this Wood Elf coming toward me.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>He was handsome, however it was his companion that held that my attention.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>A Dark Elf Necromancer was at his side.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I had never seen a necromancer, let alone a Dark Elf!<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>My heart was racing and I could feel terror rising from my stomach.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>The Wood Elf seemed to sense my panic, and motioned for his friend to stay put for a minute.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I kneeled before him, and he sat beside me.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>We chatted for a few minutes, before the Dark Elf came near.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>She was oddly beautiful, I had been certain no creature of Hate could be so beautiful.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>It didn’t take long to realize that she was not the evil I had assumed her to be.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>The introduced themselves as Noetikos and Valerene.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>They were from a guild known as Binded Souls.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Noetikos offered me membership to this guild.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I accepted, hoping that I might obtain some knowledge from this group of diverse people.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Valerene showed me many things, including the ways of baking.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>She was mentor, my friend.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I often talked with Noetikos into the wee hours of the night.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>He was a knowledgeable, and kind ranger.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>The leader of the guild was a vivacious Froglok by the name of Rikov.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Oh, and he was a goofy one, constantly making me laugh.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>It was not long before he made me an officer of the guild.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I felt so honored that he chose me for this.”<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">Her eyes darkened again, “One day, Rikov vanished.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>We did not hear from him for a long time.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Noetikos was away studying, and there were rarely any other officers around.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>The guild was getting restless, and many were thinking of leaving what had become our family.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>The idea of losing this new family pulled at my heart strings.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I created a new guild to keep them all together.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Most of the guild came with me to the new guild.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Noetikos was among the last to leave, his heart was so loyal to Rikov.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Valerene was Rikov’s fiancée, and refused to leave.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Thus, we came to be Moonlite Redemption.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>After a time, Noetikos came to lead the guild with me, at my side.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>We were great friends, and it was a good combination for a long time.”<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">Tears came to her eyes as she spoke, “I will not speak of the details of the day Noetikos left the guild, except to say that it was time for him to move on.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I miss my friend very much, but we still chat occasionally.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>It is not the same as it once was, but we are still friends.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I lead the guild alone now.”<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">It was obvious that I needed to change the subject, “What of love dear sister?<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Have you had no romantic interest in anyone?”<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">Her cheeks turned bright red, all the way to her ears.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>“There might be someone”<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>She giggled as I have not her giggle in a long time, “He is a barbarian of all things!<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>He is a warrior, and a handsome one at that.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>He is tall and muscular, and a little gruff, as most Barbarians are.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>He has kindness in his eyes however, and a warm heart.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I won’t say that Raidaman and I are involved, but I will say that it might be a possblity one day.”<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">A loud banging at the front door cut our interview short at this point.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>It was a young Dark Elf Necromancer that&nbsp;I knew well.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;I gave Uanelil a huge hug, he had always been like the an uncle I've never had.&nbsp; He whispered something in&nbsp;Amyana's ear, she smiled widely and quickly hugged me goodbye.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Off she went on her next adventure, her red hair flying behind her.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>She stopped suddenly and turned towards me, and I could barely hear her whisper “I love you Vivi” She put her helm on her head, and was gone.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span><o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt; COLOR: black; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="#d3d3d3">My sister is one of the most friendly, compassionate, and enjoyable people I have ever had the pleasure to meet.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>I have no doubt that things will turn out well for her in the end.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Who knows, perhaps, one day, she will discover the fate of our father.<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt" align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 22pt; FONT-FAMILY: Scriptina; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA"><font color="#d3d3d3">Vivicia Angeluv</font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt" align="left"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 22pt; FONT-FAMILY: Scriptina; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA"></span></span><span style="FONT-SIZE: 18pt; COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 16.5pt"><span style="mso-spacerun: yes"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="3">The preceeding hath been a recounting of the life of Amyana Angeluv.&nbsp; As her life hath yet to end, more may accompany this detailing in the near future.</font></span></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"><span style="COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik"><font color="#d3d3d3">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="6">Our Family</font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="6"></font></span>&nbsp;</p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="6">Vivicia</font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="6"></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="6"><img src="/pics/1602/hierarchy/Vivi.JPG" /></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="6">Issynal</font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik"><font color="#d3d3d3"></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 48pt; COLOR: silver; FONT-FAMILY: Magik; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"><font color="